{"skill": "Trigonometry", "difficulty": "Easy", "question": "In a right triangle, one of the acute angles measures $30^{\circ}$. The length of the side opposite this angle is 7 units.

What is the length of the hypotenuse?

", "choices": ["A) $7 \sqrt{3} \text{ units}$", "B) $14 \text{ units}$", "C) $\frac{7}{2} \text{ units}$", "D) $7 \text{ units}$"], "answer": "B", "explanation": "In a $30^{\circ}-60^{\circ}-90^{\circ}$ triangle, the hypotenuse is twice the length of the side opposite the $30^{\circ}$ angle. Therefore, if the side opposite $30^{\circ}$ is 7 units, the hypotenuse would be $2 \times 7$, or 14 units. Thus, the correct answer is B."}

